  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 709.08 Frequency of Standard Monitoring for Total Coliforms for Non-Seasonal Non-Community Water Systems and Certain Seasonal Systems",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 709.08 Frequency of Standard Monitoring for Total Coliforms for Non-Seasonal Non-Community Water Systems and Certain Seasonal Systems.\n\n(a) Subject to (b) and (c) below, and Env-Dw 709.09, the owner of an NCWS that is served solely by one or more protected water sources and that either is not a seasonal system or is a seasonal system that is described in Env-Dw 709.01(d) shall monitor for bacteria based on the number of persons served, as follows:\n\n(1) If the NCWS serves 1,000 persons or fewer per month, the owner shall collect one sample during each calendar quarter that the NCWS provides water to the public; and\n\n(2) If the NCWS serves more than 1,000 persons during any month, the owner shall take the number of samples for total coliforms per month as required for a like-sized CWS, as specified in Env-Dw 709.05(a).\n\n(b) If the number of persons served by an NCWS is event-driven, such as a racetrack, fairgrounds, or concert venue, the owner shall take the number of samples for total coliforms as a like-sized CWS as specified in Env-Dw 709.05(a), using the average daily population calculated over a one-month period.\n\n(c) An NCWS supplied by surface water or groundwater under the direct influence of surface water shall monitor for coliform bacteria monthly.\n\nSource. #9700, eff 5-1-10; ss by #10771, eff 2-1-15; ss by 14343, eff 8-22-25, EXPIRES: 8-22-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html"
